  "isolationRationale": "Whole28-case original suite reviewed, including real ephemeral127.0.0.1 encrypted server fixture and all55 unchanged module hashes shared with the standing-intent closure. Test methods (including files.watch/orchestration names) only reach a fixture dispatcher, never actual filesystem watches or authority endpoints. Original connections close timers/sockets and reject outstanding promises; afterEach closes owned servers. Keepalive intervals clear on socket close; delayed callbacks stay within test fixtures. One capped-admission case allocates3MiB parameters under original retained-byte limits. Three cases use private-state/spies or export-surface inspection, and the capped-retry case injects state; remaining observations include real socket traffic. No profiles, subprocesses or external networks.",
  "testEvidenceBoundary": "Original shared-control tests cover multiplexed requests/subscriptions, orchestration envelope field precedence, cleanup and repeated close, pending-byte release/admission, short-RPC deadlines despite keepalives, handshake replacement, reconnect/replay, local no-pong liveness termination and first-response replay tags. Server emulates RPC results and does not execute real operations. No actual SSH/Tailscale outage, OS sleep, independent crypto/mixed-version audit, remote process verdict, filesystem watch, rewritten product or packaged UI parity.",
